Virtualization & Cloud basics:
==============================
1) What is Virtualization?
--------------------------
Process of creating virtual versions of physical resources, such as servers, storage devices, or networks. By allowing multiple virtual environments to run on a single physical machine,
Virtualization maximizes hardware utilization and provides flexibility in resource management.

------------                                                               --------         ------------
Application |                                                              |  App |         |   App    |
------------                                                               --------         ------------
-----                                                                      --------         ------------
OS  |                                                                      |  OS  |         |    OS    |
-----                                                                      --------         ------------
-------------                                                              ------------------------------
Hardware    |                                                              |   Virtualization Layer     |    
-------------                                                              ------------------------------
Traditional Machine architecture                                           ------------------------------
                                                                           |           Hardware          |
                                                                           ------------------------------
                                                                             Virtual Machine Architecture

2) Types of Virtualization:
----------------------------
=> Server virtualization - Running multiple instances on a single physical server, improving resource efficiency and management
=> Desktop virtualization - Creating virtual desktops that can be accessed from various devices, enabling remote work and centralized management
=> Application virtualization - Running applications in a virtual environment separate from the underlying operating system, allowing for easier deployment and compatibility.
=> Network virtualization - Abstracting network resources to create a virtual network, enhancing network flexibility and scalability

3) Benefits of virtualization:
------------------------------
=> Resource efficiency - Better utilization of physical hardware resources, reducing waste.
=> Cost savings - Decreased hardware and operational costs by consolidating resources.
=> Scalability - Easily scale resources up or down based on demand, providing flexibility for growth.
=> Isolation - Improved security and stability by isolating environments, minimizing the impact of failures.

4) Hypervisors:
----------------
Software that enables virtualization by allowing multiple OS to run on a single physical machine.
Types:
-> Type 1 (Bare-metal): Runs directly on the hardware (e.g, VMware vSphere, Microsoft Hyper-V)
-> Type 2 (Hosted): Runs on top of an existing OS (e.g, Oracle VirtualBox)

Role: Manage VMs, allocate resources, and ensure isolation between environments.

5) Virtual Machines (VMs):
---------------------------
Software emulations of physical computers, complete with virtual hardware components like CPU, memory, and storage
Components:
=> Virtual CPU: Allocates processing power.
=> Memory: Emulates physical RAM
=> Storage: Virtual hard drives store data.
VMs are created, managed, and run using hypervisors, providing an isolated environment for applications.

6) What is cloud computing?
----------------------------
Delivery of computing services over the internet, allowing on-demand access to a shared pool of configurable resources.
Enables users to access and use computing power, storage, and applications without needing local infrastructure.

7) Benefits of cloud computing?
-------------------------------
=> Cost efficiency - Reduces the need for physical hardware and maintenance, lowering operational costs.
=> Scalability - Easily scale resources up or down based on demand, adapting to changing needs.
=> Accessibility - Access services and data from anywhere with an internet connection.
=> Disaster recovery - Enhanced data backup and recovery options, ensuring business continuity.

8) Common Cloud Provider:
--------------------------
=> AWS - Offers a broad set of global cloud-based products.
=> Microsoft Azure - Provides a range of cloud services for analytics, storage, and more.
=> Google Cloud Platform (GCP) - focuses on cloud computing, data storage, and machine learning

9) Types of cloud services:
----------------------------
=> IaaS (infrastructure-as-a-service) - Provides virtualized computing resources over the internet (eg, AWS EC2, Microsoft Azure)
=> PaaS (Platform-as-a-service) - Offers a platform for customers to develop, run, and manage applications without the complexity of building and maintaining infrastructure (eg: Google App Engine)
=> SaaS (Software-as-a-service) - Delivers software applications over the internet on a subscription basis (eg: Google Workspace, Salesforce).

10) Deployment Models:
-----------------------
=> Public cloud - Services offered over the public internet, available to anyone (eg: Azure, AWS)
=> Private cloud - Exclusive cloud infrastructure for a single organization, providing more control and security.
=> Hybrid cloud - Combines public and private clouds, allowing for data and applications to be shared between them.
=> Multi-cloud - Use of multiple cloud services from different providers to meet specific business needs, optimizing flexibility and performance.

11) Key concepts:
------------------
=> Virtualization - Technology that enables cloud computing by abstracting physical resources, allowing for better resource management.
=> Elasticity - Ability to automatically scale resources to meet changing demands, ensuring efficiency.
=> Resource pooling - Combining multiple physical resources to serve multiple consumers, enhancing efficiency and flexibility.
