The DMZ is the first line of defence. In a real pentest, compromising a DMZ machine (e.g. bWAPP or Metasploitable) is often the entry point for pivoting deeper into the internal network — exactly what this lab is designed to simulate.

5) Network adapte assignments per machine:
------------------------------------------
Each VM needs multiple network adapters added in VirtualBox — one for each zone it must communicate with, plus a bridged adapter for host/physical network access.
=> External zone machines:
        -> Bridged — physical network access
        -> DMZ Zone adapter
        -> Internal Zone adapter
=> DMZ zone machines:
        -> Bridged — physical network access
        -> External Zone adapter
        -> Internal Zone adapter
=> Internal zone machines:
        -> Bridged — Domain Controller only (for updates)
        -> DMZ Zone adapter
        -> External Zone adapter

Only the Domain Controller in the internal zone gets a bridged adapter. Other internal machines (IIS server, clients) do not have bridged access — they use DHCP from the Domain Controller instead.

